# How to cite OpenRecipes; GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository". Recipe pages show the citation each recipe's
# author asks for (citations.yaml).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenRecipes as a source, you can cite it as below. If you use a recipe, cite the work its author links on
  the recipe's page.
title: OpenRecipes
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: OpenRecipes contributors
url: https://openrecipes.ai
repository-code: https://github.com/Compounding-Intelligence/openrecipes
license: Apache-2.0
